.TH PACORPHAN 8 "2026-08-14" "pacorphan 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
pacorphan \- find orphaned packages in a pacman system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY pacorphan
.RI [ options ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
pacorphan walks the dependency graph starting from explicitly installed packages
and reports packages installed as dependencies that are no longer required
by any explicitly installed package.
It detects orphaned packages missed by \[lq]pacman \-Qdt\[rq],
including those hidden within dependency chains and circular dependencies.
.PP
By default, optional dependencies are treated as required.
Use the
.B \-O
option to ignore them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only package names without versions, suitable for piping.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-respect-optdepends
Treat optional dependencies as required,
preventing packages required solely as optional dependencies from being orphaned.
This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-ignore-optdepends
Ignore optional dependencies,
reporting packages required solely as optional dependencies as orphans.
.TP
\fB\-\-dbpath\fP \fIpath\fP
Set an alternate database location.
Defaults to the
.I DBPath
directive resolved from the pacman configuration.
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fP \fIpath\fP
Set an alternate installation root.
Defaults to the
.I RootDir
directive resolved from the pacman configuration.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fP \fIpath\fP
Set an alternate pacman configuration file.
.TP
\fB\-\-sysroot\fP \fIpath\fP
Set an alternate system root.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
Incorrect command usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
Remove all orphaned packages and their configuration files using pacman:
.RS
.EX
.RB "$ " "pacorphan \-q | sudo pacman \-Rn \-"
.EE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.MR pacman 8 ,
.MR pacman.conf 5
